  "implemented": [
    "Opaque HMAC grant secrets, hashed verifiers, redacted Debug and deterministic authorized issuance retry without lifetime extension.",
    "Exact trusted origin registration and binding conflict handling, bounded metadata admission, canonical task/issuer authority digest and installation-bound handles.",
    "Current task, owner, credential, issuer, registrar, membership, operation, recipient and expiry checks before execution and tool-ceiling discovery.",
    "Service facade and current narrow Get/Inbox/Wait support; no MCP adapter opens SQLite.",
    "Unassigned conversation reply view, explicit attributed single-task assignment, atomic consumption/revision and current-authorized matching receipt replay.",
    "Native Reply under the sender's own send permission, uniquely derived from a delivered accepted task question; late terminal/revoked task replies stay unassigned.",
    "Authenticated task inbox cursors, bounded metadata projection and catch-up; service registers a wake before reading and rechecks durable authority after waiting."
  ],
  "behavior_evidence": [
    "Thirteen initial grant tests plus three operation/identifier tests: tampered/unknown secrets, wrong call/chat/host binding, second task, wrong cid, room recipient ceiling, generic inbox denial, metadata change, exact fake-clock expiry, revoked backing/issuer/registrar, changed membership/operation scope, restore, capacity and concurrent issuance.",
    "Ten reply tests: two tasks in one conversation, unassigned/reordered routing, duplicate assignment/consumption, restart replay, cursor/task contrast, exact native question references, unknown/wrong/undelivered/ambiguous questions, terminal/revoked target retention, transactional rollback and competing assignment/consumption workers.",
    "Three new service tests: protected facade/revocation, commit between catch-up and wait for owner and grant, and reauthorization on revocation during wait.",
    "Existing workspace source tests including local native QUIC, HTTP, SIP, WebRTC, provider fixture and recovery behavior remain passing."
  ],
  "limits_of_proof": [
    "G4-008 and G4-009 remain in progress; these results do not close a numbered item, acceptance criterion or the gate.",
    "Native question tests seed the accepted task Send effect boundary. G4-010 must produce this boundary through real task Invoke admission and dispatch/reconciliation.",
    "Task Invoke, EffectGet and Recall remain explicitly unsupported at this checkpoint; grant admission is implemented before these handlers.",
    "Accepted-effect replay, lease/dispatch uncertainty, process crash/ACK tests, cancellation-at-quota reservation and task-aware provider/SMS dispatch remain open.",
    "Call/chat/host identifiers in unit fixtures test store binding isolation, not live provider provenance, network header authentication or actual host/MCP qualification.",
    "Public task SDK/HTTP/CLI/UCTP exposure, MCP transport/tools/skill, Vapi integration, selected Codex host and complete agent/app journeys remain planned items.",
    "No new task load-limit, release/package, remote deployment or live-provider qualification is claimed."
  ],
